            "content": "<!-- qualor:summary 6d581179-0227-4214-891e-fa6e0000c552 -->\n### ❌ Qualor: quality gate failed\n\n**Qualor way** · analysis ` ccfcd97e5d30 ` · **1 new issue** in this pull request\n\n| | Condition | Value | Required |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ❌ | New issues | 1 | ≤ 0 |\n| ➖ | Coverage on new code | — | skipped: fewer than 20 new lines |\n| ➖ | Duplication on new code | — | skipped: fewer than 20 new lines |\n\n**By severity:** 🔴 1 high\n\n#### Most severe new issues\n\n1. 🔴 **High** · maintainability · [` sonarjs:S1186 `](https://sonarcloud.io/organizations/sonarsource/rules?open=javascript%3AS1186&rule_key=javascript%3AS1186) · [` probe/item-25-20261124154332.js:2 `](https://ado.example.invalid/projects/6d581179-0227-4214-891e-fa6e0000c552/issues/d0dc2721-865a-42ce-84c3-fa6e0000e357)\\\n   Unexpected empty function ` 'emptyHandler' `.\n\n1 new issue is commented inline. · **[Open in Qualor →](https://ado.example.invalid/projects/6d581179-0227-4214-891e-fa6e0000c552/branches/c863b1ef-ac14-4e0a-8323-fa6e00006f09)**\n\n#### AI review\n\nOne minor finding: the pipeline comment promises a fixed scanner image tag, but the variable uses a mutable azure-dev tag. No critical or major issues found.\n\n**Findings:** 0 high · 0 medium · 1 low\n\n- Adds an Azure Pipelines YAML (` .azure-pipelines/qualor-docker.yml `) that runs the Qualor scanner image via docker run on pull requests and tags.\n- The first step checks out the pull request head, resolves the source commit and detaches HEAD to it, failing with clear messages when the commit is missing.\n- The second step runs the scanner container with the build variables passed through the environment, with the token supplied only via env.\n- The probe file ` probe/item-25-20261124154332.js ` adds an empty exported function; the analyzer already reports it, so no new finding is raised.\n\nReviewed commit: ` ccfcd97e5d30 `\n\n<details><summary>Prompt for an AI agent</summary>\n\n```text\nFix the problems below, which an AI review found in this pull request.\nThe review can be wrong: read the code first and skip a finding that does not hold.\nKeep each change small and run the tests afterwards.\n\n1. .azure-pipelines/qualor-docker.yml:22 Scanner image tag azure-dev is mutable, contradicting the comment that the tag is fixed\n   The header comment at line 14 says \"The image tag is fixed: nothing floats\", but QUALOR_SCANNER_IMAGE is set to qualor/scanner:azure-dev. A dev-channel tag is usually re-pushed when the image is rebuilt, so the same pipeline can run different scanner code over time and scan results can change without any repository edit. Pin the image to a release version or an immutable digest (repo@sha256:...), or correct the comment if a moving tag is intended.\n```\n\n</details>",
